stress.tex:
For the connected undirected analysis graph, let \(\delta_{ij}=d_G(i,j)\) denote the finite shortest-path distance between nodes \(i\) and \(j\), computed from strictly positive edge lengths \(\ell_{uv}\). We use the metric-stress objective
\begin{equation}
F_{\Delta,w}(X)
=
\sum_{i<j}w_{ij}
\left(\delta_{ij}-\|\mathbf x_i-\mathbf x_j\|\right)^2,
\qquad w_{ij}=1.
\label{eq:stress_function}
\end{equation}
Thus, the dissimilarities in the stress function and in the Guttman transform are the same quantities \(\delta_{ij}\).

The \texttt{scikit-learn} implementation uses the \textit{Scaling by MAjorizing a COmplicated Function} (SMACOF) algorithm~\cite{deleeuw1977applications, deleeuw1980multidimensional, borg2005modern}, which iteratively updates coordinates to monotonically decrease the stress $F$ in Eq.~\eqref{eq:stress_function}~\cite{kruskal1964multidimensional, pisarchik2014control}. At each iteration $t$, the algorithm computes pairwise Euclidean distances $d_{ij}(X^{(t)})$ from the current configuration and constructs a weighted Guttman transform matrix:
\begin{equation}
 B(X^{(t)})_{ij} =
 \begin{cases}
 -\,w_{ij}\,\dfrac{d^{\text{hop}}_{ij}}{d_{ij}(X^{(t)})}, & i \neq j, \\[6pt]
 \displaystyle \sum_{k \neq i} w_{ik}\,\dfrac{d^{\text{hop}}_{ik}}{d_{ik}(X^{(t)})}, & i = j.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
When $d_{ij}(X^{(t)})=0$, we replace it with a small divergence guard $\varepsilon_{0}$ (we use $\varepsilon_{0}=10^{-5}$) to avoid numerical instabilities in the construction of $B(X^{(t)})$; this is distinct from the SMACOF convergence tolerance \texttt{eps}$=10^{-6}$ used as the stopping criterion. We then apply a SMACOF majorization step with uniform weights $w_{ij}=1$ and re-center the configuration after each iteration so that $\sum_{i=1}^n x_i^{(t)}=0$. Under this convention, the update can be written as
\begin{equation}
 X^{(t+1)}=\frac{1}{n}\,B\!\left(X^{(t)}\right)X^{(t)}.
 \label{notation: convention not}
\end{equation}
For uniform weights $w_{ij}=1$, this update coincides with the Guttman transform $X^{(t+1)}=V^{+}B(X^{(t)})X^{(t)}$, where $V^{+}=\tfrac{1}{n}H$ is the Moore--Penrose inverse of the weight Laplacian $V=nH$; since $B(X^{(t)})X^{(t)}$ is already centered, the projection $H$ acts as the identity and the update reduces to Eq.~\eqref{notation: convention not}.
The stress $F(X)$ is recomputed after each update. The SMACOF majorization ensures a non-increasing stress sequence, i.e., $F(X^{(t+1)})\le F(X^{(t)})$, until convergence, maximum of 300 iterations.

